sub build | compile an entry file to a native executable
sub run | build an entry file and run it, passing on its exit code
sub test | discover and run `*_test.lu` files
sub fmt | reformat source in the one canonical style
sub fix | apply the compiler's machine-applicable suggestions
sub doc | generate the package's documentation
sub init | promote a script to a package
sub add | add a dependency to `wolf.pkg`
sub rm | remove a dependency from `wolf.pkg`
sub update | re-fetch pinned dependencies and refresh the ledger
sub audit | the capability tree, and what changed since `wolf.sum`
sub tree | the resolved dependency tree
sub why | the chain that pulls one dependency into the build
sub vendor | mirror the resolved dependencies into `vendor/wolf/`
sub publish | verify a package and emit its signed log record
sub cache | where the script cache lives, and collecting it
sub interface | print every module's public interface
sub audit-surface | the package's complete unsafety inventory
sub profile | read and merge profile-guided-optimization data
sub c-import | import C headers, and show what was refused
sub conform-run | observe one program and emit a conformance record
sub lsp | serve the Language Server Protocol over stdio
flag --explain | the full explanation of one diagnostic code
flag --version | this build's identity and its paired interpreter
flag -h --help | this message; `wolf <command> --help` for one command
flag --man | the man page, for an installer to place
flag --completions arg=none | a completion script for bash, zsh or fish
